[size=5][b]Auto Sort Inventory[/b][/size]

Tired of pressing Sort every time you pick something up? This mod keeps your [b]character inventories[/b] and [b]containers[/b] (chests, bags, etc.) sorted automatically, using the game's own sorting.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inventories and opened containers re-sort themselves whenever items are added or removed.
[*]Uses whichever option you pick from that window's [b]Sort[/b] button (Type, Value, Weight, …). Until you pick one, it uses the game's current sort.
[*]Gaps in the grid are closed automatically.
[*]Drag-and-drop still works: drop items onto the grid to move them into that inventory or container.
[*]UI-only and save-safe: it uses the game's built-in Sort action and doesn't add any items, scripts or data to your save.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Baldur's Gate 3, Patch 8 (tested on Hotfix 10, GOG version)
[*]No Script Extender needed
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/LaughingLeader/BG3ModManager/releases]BG3 Mod Manager[/url] if you don't already use it.
[*]Drag the downloaded zip into BG3 Mod Manager (or extract [i]AutoSortInventory.pak[/i] into [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Larian Studios\Baldur's Gate 3\Mods[/i] and refresh).
[*]Move [b]Auto Sort Inventory[/b] to the Active list (drag it to the left side or double-click it).
[*]Click [b]Save Load Order[/b], then start the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]
Deactivate it in BG3 Mod Manager and save the load order. Your items stay wherever the last sort put them. Nothing else is changed.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Keyboard & mouse UI only.[/b] Controller / Steam Deck layouts are not supported yet.
[*]Newly picked-up items briefly appear in the last slot before they get sorted into place.
[*]Your chosen sort option isn't saved. It may go back to the default after loading a save or reopening a window. Just pick it again.
[*]The [b]party[/b] inventory screen's Sort button doesn't change the auto-sort option (that screen still shows sorted inventories).
[*]Because items are always sorted, you can't keep a manual arrangement while the mod is active.
[*]Multiplayer hasn't been tested yet. Feedback welcome!
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Overrides the [b]container window[/b] and the [b]character inventory grid[/b]. It will conflict with other mods that replace either of those.
[*]Other UI mods that don't touch those screens (e.g. ImprovedUI) should be fine.
[*]A future game patch that changes the container window may require an update to this mod.
[/list]

